  ## Redis Justification

Redis is used for shopping carts and temporary cached data.

PostgreSQL is used for permanent business data such as users, products, orders, and payments.

Redis is useful for the shopping cart because it provides very fast read and write operations. Cart data can change frequently while the customer is shopping.

Redis also supports expiration, so temporary data can automatically expire.

Using Redis reduces the number of temporary requests that PostgreSQL needs to handle.

PostgreSQL remains the source of truth for completed orders and payments.
